Before diving into the best practices, please note that you may need to adapt the globs depending on your specific project structure.

---
name: react-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for React component development and state management
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use functional components with hooks for better performance and readability
- Implement proper state management using Context API or external libraries like Redux
- Utilize memoization with `useMemo` and `useCallback` to optimize re-renders
- Follow the single responsibility principle for components
- Use prop-types or TypeScript for type checking and better developer experience

---
name: typescript-best-practices.mdc
description: TypeScript coding standards and type safety guidelines
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
---

- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json for enhanced type checking
- Use interfaces for object shapes and types for utility types
- Leverage type inference where possible, but provide explicit types for complex scenarios
- Implement custom type guards for runtime type checking
- Use readonly and const where appropriate to prevent unintended mutations

---
name: wxt-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for developing browser extensions with WXT
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Organize your extension code into separate modules for content scripts, background scripts, and UI components
- Use WXT's built-in environment variables for browser-specific configurations
- Implement proper error handling and logging for background scripts
- Utilize WXT's hot module replacement for faster development cycles
- Follow WXT's recommended project structure for better maintainability

---
name: tailwind-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for implementing Tailwind CSS in UI/UX design
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,css}
---

- Use utility-first approach for rapid development and consistent styling
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind's responsive modifiers
- Create custom components with Tailwind's `@apply` directive for reusability
- Optimize CSS output by enabling purge mode in production
- Follow accessibility guidelines by using semantic HTML and appropriate ARIA attributes

---
name: openai-api-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for integrating and using the OpenAI API
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Implement proper error handling and rate limiting for API requests
- Use streaming responses for better performance in long-running tasks
- Cache API responses where appropriate to reduce costs and improve performance
- Implement proper security measures for API keys and sensitive data
- Follow OpenAI's usage guidelines and monitor your API usage

---
name: web-scraping-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for web scraping and data extraction
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Respect robots.txt and website terms of service
- Implement proper error handling and retries for robust scraping
- Use headless browsers for dynamic content and JavaScript-heavy websites
- Implement rate limiting and user-agent rotation to avoid being blocked
- Store and process scraped data ethically and in compliance with data protection laws

---
name: reverse-image-search-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for implementing reverse image search functionality
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use efficient image processing libraries for feature extraction and comparison
- Implement caching mechanisms for frequently searched images
- Consider using multiple search engines or APIs for more comprehensive results
- Implement proper error handling and fallback mechanisms
- Ensure compliance with copyright and image usage policies


